<main>
<p class="overline">Transcript</p>
<h1>Q4 2026 Earnings Call</h1>
<p class="meta">Alex, Chief Executive · 1 October 2026 to 16 October 2026</p>

<h2>Highlights</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Opening index</th><td class="num">96.00</td></tr>
<tr><th>Closing index</th><td class="num">90.84</td></tr>
<tr><th>Change</th><td class="num">−5.16 (−5.37%)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Quarter range</th><td class="num">88.50 to 101.25</td></tr>
<tr><th>Enough Threshold</th><td class="num">105.00</td></tr>
<tr><th>Threshold revisions</th><td class="num">4</td></tr>
<tr><th>Positions held</th><td class="num">1</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Prepared Remarks</h2>
<div class="turn operator">
<p class="speaker">Operator</p>
<p>Welcome to the Q4 2026 results call for Alex. Following prepared remarks, we will open the line for questions from analysts. I will now turn the call over to the Chief Executive, Alex.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn executive">
<p class="speaker">Alex, Chief Executive</p>
<p>Thank you, and thanks to everyone for being with us today.</p>
<p>The Personal Standing Index opened the quarter at 96.00 and closed at 90.84, a change of −5.16 points, or −5.37%. This was a challenging quarter, and the result reflects conditions across the peer set rather than any change in our underlying fundamentals.</p>
<p>The Enough Threshold was adjusted 4 times in the period, and now stands at 105.00. I would characterize that as a sign of the strength of the market.</p>
<p>I won&#x27;t pretend the quarter was without challenges. Performance in sourdough starter age, parallel parking under observation and hairline trajectory was below our expectations.</p>
<p>For the coming quarter, we are prioritizing sourdough starter age. We are also undertaking a strategic review of procedural competence, and we will update you as appropriate.</p>
<p>Across the peer set, Dana (DANA) posted a gain of 6.48 points. We congratulate them, and we are studying their results carefully.</p>
<p>The peer set expanded during the quarter with the addition of your manager&#x27;s manager.</p>
<p>The Standard Classification was extended during the quarter to include cat&#x27;s apparent affection, now reflected in our results.</p>
<p>Operator, we are now ready to take questions.</p>
</div>

<h2>Question-and-Answer Session</h2>
<div class="turn operator">
<p class="speaker">Operator</p>
<p>Our first question comes from the line of an analyst at Continental Research Partners. Please go ahead.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn analyst">
<p class="speaker">Analyst, Continental Research Partners</p>
<p>Thanks for taking the question. Could you speak to performance in sourdough starter age? It looks like Dana has widened their lead there.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn executive">
<p class="speaker">Alex, Chief Executive</p>
<p>I&#x27;d point you to the long-term trend.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn operator">
<p class="speaker">Operator</p>
<p>We will take our next question from Second Street Equities.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn analyst">
<p class="speaker">Analyst, Second Street Equities</p>
<p>I wanted to ask about parallel parking under observation. Marcus Bell appears to be well ahead. Is that structural?</p>
</div>
<div class="turn executive">
<p class="speaker">Alex, Chief Executive</p>
<p>We see that as a timing issue.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn operator">
<p class="speaker">Operator</p>
<p>The next question is from Regional Securities. Your line is open.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn analyst">
<p class="speaker">Analyst, Regional Securities</p>
<p>Can you give us any guidance on the timeline for reaching the Enough Threshold? The shortfall is currently 14.16.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn executive">
<p class="speaker">Alex, Chief Executive</p>
<p>We&#x27;re very comfortable with where we are.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn operator">
<p class="speaker">Operator</p>
<p>Our next question comes from Independent Research Associates. Please go ahead.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn analyst">
<p class="speaker">Analyst, Independent Research Associates</p>
<p>Could you comment on the performance of Dana? A gain of 6.48 points seems significant.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn executive">
<p class="speaker">Alex, Chief Executive</p>
<p>We don&#x27;t comment on individual Comparables.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn operator">
<p class="speaker">Operator</p>
<p>We will take our next question from General Brokerage Services.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn analyst">
<p class="speaker">Analyst, General Brokerage Services</p>
<p>You currently hold one position. Can you talk about your strategy there?</p>
</div>
<div class="turn executive">
<p class="speaker">Alex, Chief Executive</p>
<p>We don&#x27;t break that out.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn operator">
<p class="speaker">Operator</p>
<p>The next question is from Provincial Capital Markets. Your line is open.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn analyst">
<p class="speaker">Analyst, Provincial Capital Markets</p>
<p>Can you comment on the Spotlight readings this quarter?</p>
</div>
<div class="turn executive">
<p class="speaker">Alex, Chief Executive</p>
<p>We&#x27;ll have more to say about that next quarter.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn operator">
<p class="speaker">Operator</p>
<p>That concludes our question-and-answer session. I will turn the call back to Alex for any closing remarks.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn executive">
<p class="speaker">Alex, Chief Executive</p>
<p>Thank you all for your questions. We look forward to speaking with you next quarter.</p>
</div>
<div class="turn operator">
<p class="speaker">Operator</p>
<p>Ladies and gentlemen, that concludes today&#x27;s call. You may now disconnect.</p>
</div>

